# /etc/conf/modreg.d/z3660rtg -- the z3660rtg module package's defaults
# (amix-dlm C3-5 sec 1): one `param <name>=<value>` per default other than
# the module's own, `disable` to ship it off.  None: z3660rtg loads with its
# own defaults,
#   blit=1       use the board's blitter (0: draw on the CPU)
#   fixed=0      1: let the probe try the fixed-base rows of a board with no
#                AutoConfig entry (it reads a fixed address on any machine
#                with the right chipset; a real Z3660 has an entry)
#   kvfb=0       MiB of the framebuffer mapped for the kernel when the board
#                lies above the identity map (0: 8 on k46, 2 on k30; at most 46)
#   maxarea=0    the blit band, in pixels (0: 8192; at most 3686400)
# Local settings belong in /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/z3660rtg, which no
# package owns, as `param <name>=<value>` lines.
